      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe English Cookery Book\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 edited by JH Walsh \u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#walsh-1859\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EWalsh 1859\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E;",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EThorpe Pudding.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n907. Put a layer of preserves at the bottom of a pie-dish, and over it grated bread-crumbs three-quarters of an inch thick, pour over them a custard; bake in rather a cool oven twenty-five minutes. One quart of milk and four eggs makes custard enough for a good-sized pudding.\u003Cbr\u003E"
